    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20">

                <pb facs="0129" n="9" xml:id="pg9"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-07-21"><hi rendition="#italic">July 21,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 76, Bulgarian series.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a
                    translation of a letter from General Petroff, the Bulgarian minister of foreign
                    affairs, expressing his sympathy on the occasion of the death of Mr. Hay, of
                    which I had informed him.</p>
                <p>I have also to acknowledge the receipt of the Department’s circular of the 3d
                    instant, containing the President’s proclamation concerning the death of Mr.
                    Hay, and to report that in accordance with instructions the flag of this
                    legation was displayed at half-mast for ten days.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles S.
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d20-a1.xml" xpointer="d20-a1"/>
